This worked for me up 13.2.4, then 13.3.0 broke my use case.

FWIW, my API route takes in a multipart form request from a regular HTML form, and forwards that request to a remote endpoint by setting `content-type` and `content-length` then streaming the body.

```
export default async function handler(
  req: NextApiRequest,
  res: NextApiResponse
) {
  const testId = getStringParam("testId", req.query);
  const variantId = getStringParam("variantId", req.query);

  const upload = await fetch(`api/tests/${testId}/variants/${variantId}/upload_pdf/`, {
    method: 'POST',
    body: req, // ReadableStream
    headers: {
      "content-type": req.headers["content-type"],
      "content-length": req.headers["content-length"]
    },
    duplex: "half",
  });

  if (!upload.ok) {
    throw new Error("Upload failed.");
  }

  res.redirect(303, `/tests/${testId}/variants/${variantId}/edit`);
}

export const config = {
  api: {
    bodyParser: false
  }
};
```

This technique doesn't seem to work without `content-length`. The remote request is being handled by a Django 4.1.2 server.
